Where the outdoor temperature forecast comes from. Only used once a thermal load exists.

{profiles}

Other sources are under **Advanced settings**.

invalid_profile.description:
These profiles were skipped. Every other profile loaded normally.

{details}

Fix the file and reload the integration. The `emhass_companion.test_profile` action shows exactly what a profile produces.

sources_blind.description:
These entities have been unavailable for more than {minutes} minutes:

{entities}

{consequence}

Check the integration that provides them -- a Modbus or cloud inverter that has lost its connection is the usual cause. This repair clears itself as soon as they report again.

script_control_entity.description:
A script cannot be used to follow the plan: its state is on only while it runs, so it would be re-triggered on every apply, and turning it off would cancel the script instead of stopping the appliance. These loads are therefore not being switched at all:

{details}

Edit each load (Settings > Devices & services > EMHASS Companion > the load > Configure) and pick a switch or input_boolean instead, or clear the field and keep the load advisory-only, switching it from your own automation on its `should_run` sensor.

bad_stored_time.description:
Home Assistant could not make sense of these stored times of day, so the default was used instead:

{details}

This normally means the configuration was hand-edited or restored from a backup written by a different version. Open Settings > Devices & services > EMHASS Companion (or the load in question) and set the time again to clear this.

standard_names_taken.description:
EMHASS Companion was asked to publish under EMHASS's own entity ids, but these are already in use:

{details}

Almost always this is the EMHASS add-on publishing them itself. Those sensors keep their Companion names for now. To finish the switch, turn off publishing in EMHASS (unset `publish_prefix`, or stop calling its publish-data action), delete the leftover entities, then reload EMHASS Companion. To stop trying, turn the option off under Settings > Devices & services > EMHASS Companion > Configure > EMHASS entity names.
